            <sourceDesc>
                <msDesc>
                    <msIdentifier>
                        <repository>museum/archive</repository>
                        <idno>inventory number</idno>
                    </msIdentifier>
                    <physDesc>
                        <objectDesc>
                            <supportDesc>
                                <support>
                                    <p><rs type="execution">Mosaic</rs> inscription on the <objectType>lunette</objectType> above the entrance from the outer narthex to the inner narthex <material/><dimensions/></p>
                                </support>
                            </supportDesc>
                            <layoutDesc>
                                <layout>Inscribed on the archivolt framing the lunette; gold background, blue-gray border. The text is arranged in three lines, each line including three lines of verse; the poetic layout is clearly indicated by the spaces between each verse line, which highlight the tripartite division of the available space, and by the vertical alignment of the verses. </layout>
                            </layoutDesc>
                        </objectDesc>
                        <handDesc>
                            <handNote>Squarish thin-line majuscules with occasional accents and breathings, black letters against gold background. Oval-shaped epsilon and sigma, tau with drooping serifs, upsilon and chi with pronounced finials, low delta with horizontal bar extending beyond the triangle, delta, alpha, and lamda with decorative finial left of the apex. No ligatures. Variations of this script are found in the Deesis mosaic below: in the open book held by Christ (plainer, more squat letters) and the monograms accompanying the figures of Christ, the Virgin, and St John the Baptist (more decorative, with ligatures). <height> ca. 5,2 cm</height>
                            </handNote>
                        </handDesc>
                    </physDesc>
